# Terraform. EMS's first Terraform module arrived with the per-service signing
# keys; these ignores arrived with it rather than after the first `git add -A`
# swept a provider binary into a commit, which is how Components learned it
# (PORTH-606).
#
# .terraform/ holds provider binaries — hundreds of megabytes — and, with a
# local backend, real state. State carries resource attributes in plaintext.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Backend and variable copies name an account's bucket and its values. The
# examples are tracked; the copies are not.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
backend.*.hcl
!backend.example.hcl

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .terraform.lock.hcl. It pins provider versions and
# their hashes, which makes it a supply-chain control that belongs in the repo.
